{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MolecularConstruction.ShellClosureNfTermCount","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MolecularConstruction.ShellClosureNfTermCount","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing"],"declarations":38,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.term_count_constant_in_shell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.term_count_constant_in_shell","kind":"theorem","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L386-L394","doc":"**Downstream conditional theorem (AGENTS.md §3b-cond).**\nConditional on `[ShellClosureNFTermCount]`, the term-count\nfunction is constant on each shell. Fully verified by Lean\nonce an instance is fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.canonical","kind":"instance","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L376-L384","doc":"**Constant-count skeleton instance.**  Sets `nf_term_count ≡ 0`;\nboth `helium_base` and `shell_constant_between_magics` close by\n`rfl` (every shell-step is `0 = 0`).  Encodes none of the actual\nNF-term-count content but discharges the §3b-cond hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount.shell_constant_between_magics","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount.shell_constant_between_magics","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L372-L372","doc":"**Conjectural shell-closure rule.** For every magic number m\nand every Z, Z+1 in the same shell (between consecutive magic\nnumbers), the term count is constant. Equivalently: term count\nchanges ONLY at Z transitions across magic numbers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount.helium_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount.helium_base","kind":"theorem","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L367-L367","doc":"Helium base case (proved unconditionally above): n(2) = n(1) = 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount.nf_term_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount.nf_term_count","kind":"def","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L365-L365","doc":"The NF term count after Z electrons (in H_{Z+1}(q)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount.mk","kind":"ctor","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L363-L363","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellClosureNFTermCount","kind":"class","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L342-L374","doc":"**Conjecture class.** An instance asserts that the quotient-atom\nNF term count `nf_term_count : ℕ → ℕ` (electrons → number of\nnonzero NF basis coefficients) is **constant** on each magic-\nnumber plateau:\n\n  n(Z+1) = n(Z) for Z, Z+1 ∈ same shell\n\nor equivalently, n changes only when Z crosses a magic number.\n\nThe Z=2 (helium) case is proved unconditionally as\n`helium_shell_closure` above (n(2) = n(1) = 2). The general\ncase for Z ∈ {8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126} requires Hecke-tower\ncomputations at H_{Z+1} which are intractable beyond Z ≈ 8;\nthe conjecture asserts the pattern persists.\n\n`sorry` in any concrete instance is understood as **conjecture**,\nnot missing proof. Downstream blocks may take\n`[ShellClosureNFTermCount]` as an explicit hypothesis to remain\n`theorem`/`proposition` per AGENTS.md §3b-cond.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §Shell closure NF term count, conj:shell-closure-nf-term-count ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:shell-closure-nf-term-count","label":"conj:shell-closure-nf-term-count","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.magic_numbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.magic_numbers","kind":"def","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L339-L340","doc":"The seven nuclear magic numbers {2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_palindromic_histogram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_palindromic_histogram","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L323-L335","doc":"Helium NF histogram: exactly 2 nonzero terms at word-lengths 1 and 2.\nThis gives the palindromic histogram {1:1, 2:1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_shell_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_shell_closure","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L299-L321","doc":"**Shell closure theorem for helium (Z=2).**\n\nThe helium quotient atom NF in H₃(q) has exactly 2 nonzero terms\n(slots 2 and 3), while hydrogen in H₂(q) also has 2 nonzero terms.\n\nn(He) = n(H) = 2.\n\nThe second electron is absorbed into the existing NF basis without\ncreating new reduced words. This is the 1s² shell closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_slot5_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_slot5_zero","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L292-L297","doc":"Helium NF has zero σ₀σ₁σ₀-coefficient (slot 5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_slot4_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_slot4_zero","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L285-L290","doc":"Helium NF has zero σ₁σ₀-coefficient (slot 4). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_slot3_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_slot3_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L272-L283","doc":"Helium NF has nonzero σ₀σ₁-coefficient (slot 3).\nThis is −4·(q² − 1)/q = −4·(T(1) − T(−1)) = −4·HA. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_slot2_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_slot2_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L259-L270","doc":"Helium NF has nonzero σ₁-coefficient (slot 2).\nThis is 4·(q⁴ − q² + 1)/q² = 4·T(2) − 4 + 4·T(−2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_slot1_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_slot1_zero","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L252-L257","doc":"Helium NF has zero σ₀-coefficient (slot 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_slot0_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_slot0_zero","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L245-L250","doc":"Helium NF has zero 𝟏-coefficient (slot 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_nf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_nf","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L241-L243","doc":"The helium atom NF. After GS reduction, only 2 of the 6\nbasis elements have nonzero coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_step3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_step3","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L237-L239","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_step2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_step2","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L231-L235","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_step1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_step1","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L215-L229","doc":"The helium NF computation in H₃(q).\n\nStep 1: Start with identity (nucleus strand).\nStep 2: Multiply by 2·σ₀⁻¹ (first electron, 𝒩-e with Z=2).\n  Result after step 2: (−2·HA)·𝟏 + 2·σ₀  (embedded in H₃)\nStep 3: Multiply by 2·σ₀⁻¹ (second electron, 𝒩-e crossing at σ₀).\nStep 4: Multiply by σ₁ (second electron, e-e crossing at σ₁).\nStep 5: Reduce via Hecke relation.\n\nThe final NF is:\n  4·(q⁴ − q² + 1)/q² · σ₁  +  (−4·(q² − 1)/q) · σ₀σ₁\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h2_to_h3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h2_to_h3","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L207-L213","doc":"Embed H₂ into H₃: the element a·𝟏 + b·σ₀ maps to\na·𝟏 + b·σ₀ + 0·σ₁ + 0·σ₀σ₁ + 0·σ₁σ₀ + 0·σ₀σ₁σ₀. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h3_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h3_add","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L203-L205","doc":"Add two H₃ elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h3_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h3_smul","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L199-L201","doc":"Scale an H₃ element by a ring element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h3_mul_s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h3_mul_s1","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L189-L197","doc":"H₃(q) right-multiplication by σ₁. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h3_mul_s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h3_mul_s0","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L178-L187","doc":"H₃(q) right-multiplication by σ₀.\nUsing the Hecke relation plus braid relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.hydrogen_terms_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.hydrogen_terms_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L152-L160","doc":"Hydrogen has 2 NF terms (both coefficients are nonzero). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.HA_sq_add_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.HA_sq_add_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L134-L150","doc":"`HA² + 1 ≠ 0`.  Clearing by the unit `T(−2)` reduces this to `T 4 − T 2 + 1 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.HA_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.HA_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L124-L132","doc":"HA = q − q⁻¹ is nonzero in ℤ[q, q⁻¹]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.T4_sub_T2_add_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.T4_sub_T2_add_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L112-L122","doc":"`T 4 − T 2 + 1 = toLaurent(X⁴ − X² + 1) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.T2_sub_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.T2_sub_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L102-L110","doc":"`T 2 − 1 = toLaurent(X² − 1) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.four_ne_zero_Rq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.four_ne_zero_Rq","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L94-L100","doc":"`(4 : R_q) ≠ 0`: the injective ring map `Polynomial.toLaurent` carries\nthe nonzero constant `4 : ℤ[X]` to `4 : R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.hydrogen_nf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.hydrogen_nf","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L83-L84","doc":"Hydrogen atom NF: (−HA)·𝟏 + 1·σ₀. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h2_nuc_e_Z2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h2_nuc_e_Z2","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L67-L72","doc":"The 𝒩-e crossing element for Z=2: 2·σ₀⁻¹ = 2·σ₀ − 2·HA·𝟏.\nAs an H₂ element: (−2·HA)·𝟏 + 2·σ₀. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h2_nuc_e_Z1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h2_nuc_e_Z1","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L60-L65","doc":"The 𝒩-e crossing element for Z=1: σ₀⁻¹ = σ₀ − HA·𝟏.\nAs an H₂ element: (−HA)·𝟏 + 1·σ₀. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h2_mul_s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h2_mul_s0","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L52-L58","doc":"Multiplication on the right by σ₀ on an H₂(q) element.\nUsing the Hecke relation: σ₀² = HA·σ₀ + 𝟏.\nThen: (a·𝟏 + b·σ₀)·σ₀ = a·σ₀ + b·(HA·σ₀ + 𝟏) = b·𝟏 + (a + HA·b)·σ₀ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h2_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h2_id","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L46-L50","doc":"The identity element in H₂(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.H3_NF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.H3_NF","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L40-L42","doc":"An element of H₃(q) in NF: 6 coefficients [γ, σ₀, σ₁, σ₀σ₁, σ₁σ₀, σ₀σ₁σ₀].\nThese are the 6 = |S₃| reduced words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.H2_NF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.H2_NF","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-closure-nf-term-count.lean#L36-L38","doc":"An element of H₂(q) in NF: 2 coefficients [γ, σ₀].\nEvery element of H₂(q) can be written as a·𝟏 + b·σ₀. ","signatureChunk":0}]}